// redundancy.proto — WHAT ONE `testrun redundancy` MEASUREMENT OR REPORT DOES.
//
// A test case may be removed only if the cases that remain catch every bug it
// catches, and "catches" is measured by mutants killed (owner ruling,
// 2026-10-14). `testrun redundancy` is the one tool that measures it; this is
// its request, which the daemon hands the workspace's runner whole
// (agentrepl.v1.RunRedundancy). Every field is one of the tool's flags,
// documented in modules/app/agent-repl/AGENTS.md, "Which tests are redundant".
//
// Every path is RELATIVE TO THE REPOSITORY ROOT, as a selection's is, except
// `out_dir`, which is absolute: the measurement writes outside the checkout.
// An unset optional field takes the tool's own default.

